      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "FGF21 mimetics are a promising therapeutic tool, believed to exert their anti-obesity effect partly through browning of white fat. Véniant et al. (2015) and Samms et al. (2015) present evidence arguing against fat browning as the primary mechanism causal to weight loss following FGF21-based treatment in mice."
